# INV-10 — invented. Eight overs a side: an ordinary match, scored to the last ball.
# Edge cases: an over of six dots and a wide (no maiden: the wide is the
# bowler's); a true maiden; wickets on the fifth and sixth balls of an over,
# the new batter at the non-striker's end after the change of ends; bowlers
# in spells (three, three, one, one; three, three, two); four batters who did
# not bat; a chase of 58 won off the last ball of the last over.
